 ## Overview
-Frequency Domain Shear-Warp Volume Rendering is a method that performs the shear transformation of the shear-warp factorization in the frequency domain using the shifting theorem, allowing for arbitrary, view-independent sampling distances along viewing rays via zero-padding interpolation [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard shear-warp algorithms where sampling distance is coarse and view-dependent, this technique decouples sampling density from the viewing direction by resampling in the frequency domain, thereby avoiding the large spatial zero-padding required by spatial-domain shear methods [S1, unofficial].
